/target
**/node_modules
infra/cdk.out
infra/*.js
infra/*.d.ts
.env
.DS_Store
._*

# The vendored Pyodide runtime and wheels: multi-megabyte binaries fetched by
# assets/gen-ai/vendor-pyodide.mjs. Not committed — too large for git, and the
# commit still fully determines what ships through the pinned PYODIDE_VERSION
# and WHEELS list in workbench.js plus the lockfile kept below, the same shape
# as package-lock.json plus node_modules. CI runs the vendor script before
# synth so the deploy is reproducible from a commit without the bytes in git.
/assets/gen-ai/pyodide/*
# Keep the lockfile: it is the text record of exactly what the binaries are,
# so a resolve is reproducible and reviewable even though the wheels are not
# in the repo.
!/assets/gen-ai/pyodide/pyodide-lock.json

# Reference material only, kept locally. Git tracked this as a gitlink because
# it carries its own .git directory, so its contents were never committed
# anyway. Deliberately excluded: it contains a real phone number, a personal
# email address, and an old Firebase API key, none of which belong in a repo
# that will be public. Everything worth keeping was extracted into
# content/resume.json and .kiro/roadmap/phase0/.
/.kiro/old-resume/
